<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mithridatic Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">89–<a href="/years/63-bce">63 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mithridatic Wars were three wars fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a> from 89 to 63 BCE. Mithridates overran Roman Asia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> in 88 BCE but was driven back by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a>, and later fought Murena, Lucullus and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>. After his final defeat he killed himself in 63 BCE, and Pontus was made a Roman province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mithridatic-wars.jpg" alt="Mithridatic Wars" width="320" height="268" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Javierfv1212 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PonticKingdom.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
